{# `#`, not `!`. Junos's line comment is `#`; `!` is EOS syntax and is a
   syntax error here. It is not cosmetic: `load` fails at line 1, then error
   recovery skips ahead to the next token it can resynchronise on, so the
   configuration loads PARTIALLY and reports "load complete (2 errors)" rather
   than refusing. Measured against the lab's vSRX. The sibling srl/*.j2
   templates use `#` too, and carry a trap of their own: no quote characters
   in a comment, because sr_cli tokenises quotes first. #}
# Rendered by Infrahub for {{ node }} -- do not edit.
{% include "interfaces.j2" %}
{% include "routing-options.j2" %}
security {
{% if tcp_mss %}
    /*
     * Clamp TCP to what the path behind this firewall can actually carry.
     * Two limits apply and the fabric's is the tighter: this interface's
     * 9192 - 14 (Ethernet) allows 9138, but traffic onward into a tenant VRF
     * crosses the EVPN fabric as VXLAN, which adds 50 bytes against a 9214
     * underlay: 9214 - 50 (VXLAN) - 20 (IP) - 20 (TCP) = {{ tcp_mss }}. At 9138 the
     * full-size segments were dropped inside the fabric with nothing
     * reported, and only small replies ever arrived.
     */
    flow {
        tcp-mss {
            all-tcp {
                mss {{ tcp_mss }};
            }
        }
    }

{% endif %}
{% include "address-book.j2" %}
{% include "zones.j2" %}
{% include "policies.j2" %}
}
{% include "applications.j2" %}
{% include "snmp.j2" %}
